BEHAVIOR parse-addr

DESCRIPTION
  Parses a null-terminated dotted-decimal IPv4 string ("a.b.c.d") into a packed
  int in network order (octet 0 in the low byte), suitable for make-sockaddr's
  ip input. ok = 1 if exactly 4 octets were seen, else 0 (no per-octet range
  validation).

CONTRACT
  INPUT s bytes 256
  OUTPUT ip int 8
  OUTPUT ok int 8
  GUARANTEES pure no_alloc writes_output

HASH 4469b343

IMPLEMENTATION
  acc = 0
  octet = 0
  shift = 0
  i = 0
  count = 0

  LABEL loop
    c = LOAD s 1 i
    cz = IEQ c 0 1
    BRANCH cz finish notend

  LABEL notend
    cu = AND c 255 8
    isdot = IEQ cu 46 8
    BRANCH isdot dotsep digit

  LABEL digit
    d = ISUB cu 48 8
    octet = IMUL octet 10 8
    octet = IADD octet d 8
    i = IADD i 1 8
    JUMP loop

  LABEL dotsep
    contrib = SHL octet shift 8
    acc = OR acc contrib 8
    shift = IADD shift 8 8
    octet = 0
    count = IADD count 1 8
    i = IADD i 1 8
    JUMP loop

  LABEL finish
    contrib = SHL octet shift 8
    acc = OR acc contrib 8
    count = IADD count 1 8
    STORE ip acc 8
    isok = IEQ count 4 8
    STORE ok isok 8
END
